==Campaign period==
===Issues===
With forecasts suggesting an easy reelection for Soares, plus with [[Prime Minister of Portugal|Prime Minister]] [[Aníbal Cavaco Silva|Cavaco Silva]]'s endorsement of the incumbent President's bid, the campaign was mostly stirred by the ''Macau Fax'' case.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://rr.pt/noticia/presidenciais-2016/2016/01/15/bau-das-presidenciais-quando-cavaco-apoiou-soares/44337/|title=Baú das Presidenciais. Quando Cavaco apoiou Soares |language=pt |work=Renascença|date=15 January 2016 |access-date=28 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/caso-do-fax-de-macau-3/|title=Caso do “Fax de Macau” |language=pt |work=RTP|date=4 January 1991 |access-date=28 June 2026}}</ref> The case involved the then-[[governor of Macau]], [[Carlos Melancia]], a close friend of Mário Soares, who was accused of corruption and of receiving bribes to benefit a company in the construction of the [[Macau International Airport|territory's new airport]], with copies of the faxes from the proceedings being leaked to the press.<ref name="SOL91">{{cite news |url=https://sol.iol.pt/2017/01/07/macau-o-maior-embaraco-da-vida-politica-de-soares |title=Macau, o maior embaraço da vida política de Soares |language=pt |work=SOL|date=7 January 2017 |access-date=28 June 2026}}</ref> During a debate on [[RTP1]], CDS candidate [[Basílio Horta]] used the case to attack Soares' integrity and accuse him of being involved, while Soares vehemently denied any involvement.<ref name="SOL91" /><ref>{{cite news |url=https://arquivos.rtp.pt/conteudos/presidenciais-91-debate-entre-basilio-horta-e-mario-soares-parte-i/ |title=Presidenciais 91: Debate entre Basílio Horta e Mário Soares – Parte I |language=pt |work=RTP|date=6 December 1990 |access-date=28 June 2026}}</ref>

